# Usage

The Maven Clean Plugin removes the files and directories that Maven generates during a build. Other plugins can generate more files. The Clean Plugin assumes that these files are in the `target` directory.

Clean a Maven project from the command line
-----------------------------------------------

You can run the Clean Plugin from the command line. You do not need more configuration. To run the Clean Plugin, use this command:

```unknown
  mvn clean:clean
```

The first `clean` is the alias of the plugin. The second `clean` is the goal.

The Clean Plugin is bound to a lifecycle phase called `clean`. Thus, you can also run it with this command:

```unknown
  mvn clean
```

You can also add other phases or goals:

```unknown
  mvn clean package site
```

Run the Clean Plugin automatically during a build
-----------------------------------------------------

If you cannot add `clean` to the command line, put the Clean Plugin in the `pom.xml` of a project. Then it runs each time that the project builds. The sample `pom.xml` below runs the Clean Plugin in the `initialize` phase each time that the project builds:

```unknown
<project>
  [...]
  <build>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <artifactId>maven-clean-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <executions>
          <execution>
            <id>auto-clean</id>
            <phase>initialize</phase>
            <goals>
              <goal>clean</goal>
            </goals>
          </execution>
        </executions>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
  [...]
</project>
```
